{"qid":"Q145","names":["United Kingdom"],"title":"United Kingdom","endonym":{"native":"United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland","lang":"en-gb"},"capsule":"The United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland in its current form dates from 1922, when the Irish Free State withdrew from the previous United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland following the Anglo-Irish Treaty of 1921, leaving Northern Ireland as the residual component. From 1922 onward the UK governed a rapidly decolonizing global empire—independence of India and Pakistan in 1947 marked the decisive shift—while at home constructing the National Health Service (1948) and a welfare state. Membership in the European Economic Community (from 1973) and its successor the EU lasted until Brexit took formal effect on 31 January 2020, the most significant constitutional change of the late period.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The UK's metropolitan boundaries are precisely attested; the dataset entry presumably represents the home islands rather than the full extent of empire, though Cliopatria geometry choices on colonial holdings vary.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: United Kingdom","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Kingdom"},{"label":"Britannica: United Kingdom — History","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/United-Kingdom/History"},{"label":"Britannica: British Empire","url":"https://www.britannica.com/topic/British-Empire"}],"britannica":"place/Great-Britain-island-Europe","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Great Britain","rulers":[{"qid":"Q134982","name":"David Lloyd George","start":1916,"end":1922,"imag